  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.4-rc.5: fixes a regression in rc.4's tiebreaker that broke the asymmetric-announce case. The rc.3+rc.4 rule \"drop unconditionally if tiebreaker loses\" was wrong: when only the larger peer announces, the smaller peer dropped the incoming offer-relay and the larger peer's pending offer timed out unanswered. `P2PSwarm.TwoTab_PeerDiscovery` failed ~50% of the time when coord and worker peer_ids ordered the wrong way. rc.5 changes the rule to \"first-claim wins, tiebreaker only on conflict\": the slot accepts the first arriving handler unconditionally; if the slot is later claimed by the OTHER path (HandleOfferAsync vs HandleAnswerAsync), the cross-side-stable tiebreaker decides whether to REPLACE (we are the canonical side per tiebreaker) or DROP (existing claim is canonical). Same-type conflicts (e.g. two trackers each delivering an offer-relay for the same remote) still drop the second-arriver. Both peers converge on the same PC pair: offerer-side at the smaller peer_id, answerer-side at the larger. CrossTrackerDedupRegistry now stores SimplePeer references in slots so the replace path can dispose the displaced peer; Release uses ReferenceEquals to ensure a stale OnClose doesn't free a replaced slot. Same WebSocketTracker plumbing as rc.4 — single registry per (info_hash, local_peer_id) shared across every tracker subscription. See `Docs/protocol-reference/08-offer-pairing-and-dedup.md`.",
